From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Prather <christian@agencytool.company>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period

Backport of CVE-2026-98432 fix (upstream e3f33b0a1d89 / stable 95a8c8fa) for
the L4T R38 / linux-noble-nvidia-tegra 6.8 kernel. Use kfree_rcu() at both IPv4
option free sites so a concurrent SYNACK reader cannot hit a use-after-free.

Fixes: 079096f103fa ("tcp/dccp: install syn_recv requests into ehash table")
Link: https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-98432
Signed-off-by: Christian Prather <christian@agencytool.company>
CVE: CVE-2026-98432
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=e3f33b0a1d89d738e2b913dab519226eaf76e15b]
---
--- a/net/ipv4/af_inet.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/af_inet.c
@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(sk->sk_wmem_queued);
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(sk_forward_alloc_get(sk));
 
-	kfree(rcu_dereference_protected(inet->inet_opt, 1));
+	kfree_rcu(rcu_dereference_protected(inet->inet_opt, 1), rcu);
 	dst_release(rcu_dereference_protected(sk->sk_dst_cache, 1));
 	dst_release(rcu_dereference_protected(sk->sk_rx_dst, 1));
 }
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_ipv4.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_ipv4.c
@@ -1218,7 +1218,7 @@
  */
 static void tcp_v4_reqsk_destructor(struct request_sock *req)
 {
-	kfree(rcu_dereference_protected(inet_rsk(req)->ireq_opt, 1));
+	kfree_rcu(rcu_dereference_protected(inet_rsk(req)->ireq_opt, 1), rcu);
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_TCP_MD5SIG
